    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "There are nine houses in a row on Deer Street. At least two people live in every house. There are no two neighbouring houses where more than ten people live altogether. What is the maximum number of people who can live in the nine houses?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "96"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "49"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "48"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "47"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "46"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pair up the houses",
        "body": "Group the houses as (1,2), (3,4), (5,6), (7,8) and house 9 on its own. Each pair of neighbours has at most 10 people: at most 40. House 9 has a neighbour (house 8) with at least 2 people, so house 9 has at most 8. Total at most $40 + 8 = 48$.\n\nThis is possible: 8, 2, 8, 2, 8, 2, 8, 2, 8 (every pair of neighbours has exactly 10, and $5 \\cdot 8 + 4 \\cdot 2 = 48$).\n\n**Answer: (C) 48**"
      }
    ],
