        "key": "C",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "12"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equation",
        "body": "Let Dana be $x$ years old now. Then $x + 16 = 5(x - 4)$, so $x + 16 = 5x - 20$, $4x = 36$, $x = 9$. She turns 16 in $16 - 9 = 7$ years.\n\n**Answer: (B) 7**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Think in gaps",
        "body": "The time between \"four years ago\" and \"in 16 years\" is 20 years. Her age then is 5 times her age four years ago, so the difference, 20 years, is 4 times her age four years ago: she was 5, so now she is 9 and turns 16 in 7 years.\n\n**Answer: (B) 7**"
      }
    ],
