    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Estimate with a cube root",
        "body": "The product is $8 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 91 = 19656$. Three consecutive numbers have a product close to the cube of the middle one, and $27^3 = 19683$, so try $26 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 28$: $26 = 2 \\cdot 13$, $27 = 3^3$, $28 = 2^2 \\cdot 7$, product $2^3 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 13$ ✓.\n\nSum $26 + 27 + 28 = 81$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 81**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Group the prime factors",
        "body": "One number must contain the factor 13 and one the factor 7; with $3^3 = 27$ in the middle, 26 and 28 are its neighbours, and indeed $26 \\cdot 27 \\cdot 28$ uses exactly the factors $2 \\cdot 13$, $3^3$, $2^2 \\cdot 7$. Sum 81.\n\n**Answer: (C) 81**"
      }
    ],
